column58:
In builder.py line ~519, when a read-only ELF binary needs to be stripped, the original file mode is stored using oct():

{noformat}files_that_need_chmod[file_destination_path] = oct(file_destination_path.stat().st_mode){noformat}

Later at line ~374, chmod() parses the mode string:

{noformat}path.chmod(int(mode, 8)){noformat}

oct() returns strings like {{'0o100755'}}. int('0o100755', 8) raises ValueError because base-8 int() parsing does not accept the {{0o}} prefix. This crashes whenever a read-only ELF binary is stripped and has no explicit permissions set in install.json (which would overwrite the oct() value before chmod is called).

*Fix:* Store the raw integer mode (file_destination_path.stat().st_mode) and call path.chmod(mode) directly, or use int(mode, 0) which auto-detects the base from the prefix.

column278:
In builder.py line ~1906, the has_debian_packages variable is overwritten on each loop iteration instead of being accumulated:

{noformat}has_debian_packages = False
for architecture in build_architectures:
    has_debian_packages = len(list(filter(None, app.packages[architecture].debian_packages))){noformat}

When building for multiple architectures (e.g. {{[x64, arm64]}}), only the last architecture's result is retained. If {{x64}} has debian packages but {{arm64}} does not, has_debian_packages evaluates to {{0}} (falsy). The AptHelper context manager is not initialized, and the build silently skips downloading packages for all architectures.

*Fix:* Use has_debian_packages = has_debian_packages or len(...) or refactor with any().

