20/Feb/26 2:07 PM;712020:3715a56a-506d-4b3d-9204-259adc951914;Hi [~accountid:712020:0a53f544-6c21-42a8-a85f-f6e0aad28b0a]

# I have checked OS 12.7.5 on the L14 Gen6 (AMD) (IGEL-1167), the device does *not* go into suspend when closing the lid. But there was no overlapping and the internal display did not remain dark.
#  The registry key is being used by the igel-system-tray, specifically the LidHelper: [https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/display/src/helpers/LidHelper.cpp#67|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/display/src/helpers/LidHelper.cpp#67]

In LidHelper.cpp a function decides whether suspend is allowed or not ([https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/display/src/helpers/LidHelper.cpp#93|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/display/src/helpers/LidHelper.cpp#93]). That function contains logic which disallows suspend when an external monitor is active (if I understand it correctly): 

{code:c++} // One internal and at least one external which is enabled
    if(std::find_if(displays.begin(), displays.end(), isBuiltin) != displays.end() &&
       std::any_of(displays.begin(), displays.end(), [](const auto &display) { return !display.isBuiltIn && !display.isDisabled; } ) )
    {
      return false;
    }{code}

The LidHelper was part of this feature ticket: [https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/LX8-8066|https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/LX8-8066|smart-link] (suppress suspend with external monitor active is also mentioned) - maybe this is expected behavior?

