the app-binary reads the new app-parameter {{app.igel_secure_kiosk.settings.access_only_default_directory}}
and write this param-value to the existing base_system-paramter {{userinterface.gtk.filechooser.lock_to_startup_folder}}

Therefore, the user or the admin can set the app-parameter and on every start-up of the app, the base_system-parameter will get the value from the app-parameter and the gtk-filechooser-patch does its thing as before.

column58:
If a URL is saved in setup and it contains an “&”, it will be return incorrect in getvalue via python3.

Example: {{https://www.example.com?foo=1&bar=2}}

Saved in setup.ini as {{https://www.exmple.com?foo=1&ampbar=2}}


* Correct after close and open in setup (&amp will be & again)
* Correct with getsetup get in bash (&amp is decoded to &)
* Incorrect in python3 with setup.getvalue (&amp is &amp. No decode)

