column365:
23/Dec/25 10:19 AM;712020:85e8a75a-9b53-4648-834d-8676d27c8ecd;[~accountid:712020:289f037f-8785-42c6-b39d-21c4f6346eef] as discussed regarding the [https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/APPS-3682|https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/APPS-3682|smart-link] ticket. I reproduced the issue shown in the video and gathered the logs. I tested on the HP Elite mt645 G8 Mobile, installing base_system-12.7.3+DEV and cwa-25.8.0+1. Each time after reboot, on the first launch of the Citrix session, clicking Cancel triggers the notification “Invalid credentials - try relogin…” repeatedly, even after 20+ attempts.

!image-20251223-090701.png|width=722,alt="image-20251223-090701.png"!

If I log in with the account, log off, and then relaunch the Citrix session, I can reproduce the issue after the first Cancel. After clicking Cancel, the {{storebrowse --enumerate}} process remains active in the background.

I tried terminating the process tree {{storebrowse --enumerate ...}}, {{login.py --session_instance -id 0}}, and {{cwa0}}, then relaunching the session, but the login UI does not appear.

After checking the running processes, I also killed the {{selfservice.ctx --background}} process, which allowed the login UI to reappear. Then, clicking Cancel again results in the notification “Invalid credentials - try relogin…” each time.

{quote}When the process gets stuck and I try to launch a different session (lx2402), it notifies me that the initial session (lx2203) is starting (which is normal behavior - i didn’t reproduced this in the current logs). If I attempt to launch the same initial session (lx2203) again, I no longer see the login UI, and in the {{journalctl -f}}, I can see:

{{Dec 22 13:53:51 ITCBC24110B3D65 Thunar[34061]: Starting with command: /bin/systemctl --user is-active igel-appwrap-cwa-cwa0.service && /config/bin/appwrap_alt_cmd cwa-cwa0 || /bin/systemctl --user start igel-appwrap-cwa-cwa0.service}}
{{Dec 22 13:53:51 ITCBC24110B3D65 Thunar[34067]: inactive}}
{{Dec 22 13:53:51 ITCBC24110B3D65 appwrap[34061]: Starting cwa0 as app systemd service}}
{{Dec 22 13:53:51 ITCBC24110B3D65 Thunar[34069]: active}}{quote}

