{quote}(igel-secure-kiosk:146589): {color:#ff5630}*CRITICAL*{color} **: 14:01:41.183: void webkit_settings_set_user_agent(WebKitSettings *, const char *): assertion 'WebCore::isValidUserAgentHeaderValue(userAgentString)' {color:#ff5630}*failed*{color}{quote}

The source implementation of this function, in WebKit/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitSettings.cpp

{noformat}void webkit_settings_set_user_agent(WebKitSettings* settings, const char* userAgent)
{
....(some settings check)....
String userAgentString;
if (userAgent && *userAgent) {
    userAgentString = String::fromUTF8(userAgent);
    g_return_if_fail(WebCore::isValidUserAgentHeaderValue(userAgentString));
} else
    userAgentString = WebCore::standardUserAgent(emptyString());
...(this and that something) ....
}{noformat}

WebCore::isValidUserAgentHeaderValue(userAgentString)
is interesting. I will look into this.

column58:
After a fresh startup of IgelOS-12 (here: 12.7.2 PR 1 DEV) there is a file at /config/setupd, which contains: {{/services/cwa/usr/sbin/config.py authman}}

After a reboot this directory should be empty. Content may lead to surprising side-effects.

Logs attached.

cwa app build from current master branch with: 

{noformat}.../cwa$ igelpkg build -r 12.7 -a x64 -sp -k -l{noformat}

fails with “Error: SSLCertVerificationError connecting to [https://lx2203.lx.test:|https://lx2203.lx.test:] CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED 20 unable to get local issuer certificate”

Same app works if built for IgelOS-12.5 with:

{noformat}.../cwa$ igelpkg build -r 12.5 -a x64 -sp -k -l{noformat}

Logs of package build and runtime error are attached.

For the mt645 G8, the taskbar disappears whenever settings are changed which require a restart of the desktop (for example proxy settings).

These settings trigger a “loginctl --no-ask-password terminate-user user” call, after which the desktop is reloaded, but the taskbar never shows up. The issue can also be seen by just executing this command directly in the Terminal.

In “igel-notify-ui.log” I find the following lines:

{noformat}[2025-09-23 09:36:55.767 UTC] [140695919160320] [Debug] [igel-notify-ui] [Configuration]: Value of key 'windowmanager.wm0.variables.taskbarxineramamonitor' is: Primary
[2025-09-23 09:36:55.767 UTC] [140695919160320] [Error] [igel-notify-ui] [TaskbarConfig]: Failed parsing taskbar position 'Primary': basic_string::substr: __pos (which is 8) > this->size() (which is 7){noformat}

This seems to match with the [following lines|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/libigelcommon/browse/libigel-window-common/src/TaskbarConfig.cpp#53] in the code (“libigelcommon/libigel-window-common/src/TaskbarConfig.cpp”):

{noformat}if(auto value = config.read_string(taskbarMonitorKey); value)
  {
    // The config parameters are "monitor-0", "monitor-1", ...
    std::string prefix("monitor-");
    if(value->rfind(prefix, 0) )
    {
      try {
        taskbarMonitor = std::stoi(value->substr(prefix.size() ) );
        //make the monitor id 1 based
        ++taskbarMonitor;
      } catch (const std::logic_error &err) {
        logger.log(igel::log::Level::Error, "TaskbarConfig") << "Failed parsing taskbar position '" << *value << "': " << err.what();
      }
    }
  }{noformat}

It seems that the {{if(value->rfind(prefix, 0))}} statement does not work as intended, as it’s letting through the value {{Primary}} but then cannot handle it in the substr call as it expects a different prefix. From what I can find, the {{rfind}} function returns the index at which it finds the prefix, or -1 if not found. The if-statement will therefore be False if 0 is returned (i.e. if the prefix was found), but be True if anything else is returned. 

I’m still not sure if these lines are related to the issue, as I see the error in all three versions, but the error only occurs with 12.7.x and not in 12.8.. So while it’s still an error it might be unrelated to this specific issue, but I wanted to mention it anyway.

h3. Environment

IGEL OS Version: 12.7.1, 12.7.2-1.rc.11+DEV, 12.8.0+nightly.20250922.DEV

Device Model: mt645 G8 (have also been seen by QA in VMs before)

column278:
in /config/sessions/avd/avd1, the following snippet appears:


{noformat}if test -n "/etc/avd/"; then
    test -n "$LD_LIBRARY_PATH" && LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$LD_LIBRARY_PATH":
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$LD_LIBRARY_PATH"/etc/avd/
fi{noformat}

while the correct path should be:


{noformat}export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$LD_LIBRARY_PATH":/etc/avd/{noformat}

