The check for changed git files fail when the config.param.locale is a new file.

{noformat}# Returns 0 if any of the files have been modified, 1 otherwise.
git_files_changed() {
  # Running `git diff --quite` implies `--exit-code`.
  ! git diff --quiet "$@"
}{noformat}



Git diff --quiet return 0 if the file did not exist before, therefore, the git_files_changed() always return 1 in this case.

