column58:
I have Windows OS installed on the company’s laptop and I am using IGEL OS from UD-pocket

The Windows OS is managed by IGEL and its time zone is set to UTC (no location based timezone). After booting in Windows, then back in IGEL OS, the time on the laptop is still UTC and I had to correct it with:

{noformat}ntpdate time.nist.gov{noformat}

when this happens and a time leap is detected the VPN service stops and I have to restart it manually.

The journalctl logs are attached.

{noformat}Feb 06 16:08:59 UDP85641000G776240046 nm-openvpn[22784]: SIGTERM[hard,init_instance] received, process exiting{noformat}

The moment when the time leap is detected:

{noformat}Feb 06 16:08:56 UDP85641000G776240046 igel-dsad[599]: time leap detected; reload licenses
Feb 06 14:08:45 UDP85641000G776240046 systemd-udevd[655]: Configuration file /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-libgphoto2-6.rules is marked executable. Please remove executable permission bits. Proceeding anyway.{noformat}

Log creation seems to be broken:

{{Connection failure: Connection refused}}

{{pa_context_connect() failed: Connection refused}}

the X protocol seems to deliver the resource name with a starting ‘#' in the string. However, the ica connection center does not display that '#’.

Please remove it from the resource name. 

wrong : {{#Fus $S1-2}}

correct: {{Fus $S1-2}}

[
   {
      "active_resources" : [
         {
            "PID" : 43278,
            "resource_name" : "#Fus $S1-2"
         }
      ],
      "discovery_url" : "",
      "server_url" : "[https://citimp-srv.lx.test/citrix/storeweb|https://citimp-srv.lx.test/citrix/storeweb]",
      "session_instance_id" : "",
      "session_name" : "",
      "session_type" : "browser"
   }
]

If I call: /services/cwa/sessionhandler/logoff --resource "#Fus $S1-2" nothing happens. 

----

The issue here is to handle app resources with terminate() and desktop resources with signout()/disconnect().

Additionally: Remove 10x 0.5sec polling and add 5s permanent polling.

X11 event handling was improved also.

