column58:
Analyze, why the following is not working:

{noformat}TEST(JsonSerializer, DeserializePathMap)
{
  std::string content = R"({
  "name": "IGEL path map",
  "values": {
    "key1": "Value1",
    "key2": "Value2",
    "test1": "result1",
    "test2": "result2",
    "bla": {
      "blubb": "Value3"
    }
  },
})";

  std::string error;
  igel::serialize::json::Serializer serializer;
  auto data = serializer.fromMemory<DataPathMap>(content, &error);

  ASSERT_EQ("", error);
  EXPECT_EQ("IGEL path map", data.name);
  EXPECT_EQ(5, data.values.size() );
  EXPECT_EQ("Value1", data.values.at({"key1"}) );
  EXPECT_EQ("Value2", data.values.at({"key2"}) );
  EXPECT_EQ("result1", data.values.at({"test1"}) );
  EXPECT_EQ("result2", data.values.at({"test2"}) );
  EXPECT_EQ("{ \"blubb\": \"Value3\" }", data.values.at({"bla"}) ); // wie sinnvoll ist diese Zeile? Gefühlt nicht sonderlich
  // warum funktioniert das nicht:
  // EXPECT_EQ("Value3", data.values.at({"bla", "blubb"}) );
}{noformat}

from
[https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/libigelserialize/browse/test/src/JsonSerializerTest.cpp#516-539|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/libigelserialize/browse/test/src/JsonSerializerTest.cpp#516-539]

PathMap means: {{std::map<std::vector<std::string>, std::string> values;}}
A list of strings pointing to one string.
Assumption: missing recursion, to go deeper into the object

The other way round, serialization, is working, see:
[https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/libigelserialize/browse/test/src/JsonSerializerTest.cpp#1125-1174|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/libigelserialize/browse/test/src/JsonSerializerTest.cpp#1125-1174]

column364:
07/Jan/25 4:10 PM;712020:ae26aad8-d2cf-440f-adae-bda0606aa3ae;We will not add back the old public key because it is gone for good and replaced with the new method. The deployment is the same as fr our partners and we do not want to add it back there and a second deployment is not worth the effort as it can easily be configured outside of the deployment.

There are two options either use a igelpkg < 1.0 to verify apps build with the old SDK key or add the config snippet manually by utilizing the {{config.d}} folder.

On your test machine/container just include the cert and add it to the list of verified certificates with:

{noformat}{
  "verify": [
    "<path_to_the_cert>"
  ]
}{noformat}

As it is a config snippet it will survive any updates and does not interfere with any file deployed by the app itself. When merging the config lists are always joined.

