column58:
At the moment, shared libraries are all configured via /etc/ld.so.conf.d but we never introduced proper ordering in there, it’s basically alphanumeric. As a result, app-specific libraries can overwrite system libraries, wreaking havoc.

{quote}This happened when updating from 12.4.2 to 12.5.0.rc5 with an older version of libvirt installed which in turn had its own libxml2.so depending on libicuuc.so.66 which doesn’t exist in OS 12.5. As a result, the system wasn’t able to boot into the desktop and required manual intervention to get it to a state where the old libvirt app could be removed.{quote}

A temporary solution would be to make sure that system library paths *are always configured via /etc/ld.so.conf* which has top priority over every entry in /etc/ld.so.conf.d. Ultimately, we need to prevent apps from overwriting anything in the system but that will require a GPB-level feature ticket.

