With the future version of AVD/CPC/RDP where we need to support the MSAL (Microsoft Authentication Library) we need the libubsan1 debian package since MSAL is linked against this library. But unfortunately this library does not come with license information it seems (or maybe with license information in a format we don’t expect). Therefore the build of the related app aborts with this message:

{{Error [Builder]: No license information for debian package libubsan1}}


How can we circumvent that? I understand that a package should have a license. But when a thirdparty debian packages has no license information and we have no choice and aren’t able using a different library, how should we proceed then?

