column369:
29/Aug/24 7:04 PM;712020:e5969b12-1f21-45a9-9640-332ecba73608;{noformat}std::string mimeBrowserKey = "app." + defaultBrowser + ".mimetype.mime_browser";
std::string mimeBrowserValue = setup.getValue(mimeBrowserKey);
std::string mimeSetting = "xdg-settings set default-web-browser " + mimeBrowserValue;{noformat}

Something is fishy in these lines. The command {{xdg-settings set default-web-browser}} does not need more than {{<name>.desktop}} as argument. And it is being fed with what ever is found in the registry in {{"app." + defaultBrowser + ".mimetype.mime_browser";}} The entire mechanism of checking what is the default browser (If I understood correctly) by iterating over {{app.}} and checking for a specific field is prone to error. Should be an independent entry in registry that has to be set IMO. [~accountid:712020:7a6ceaa6-9c04-4a3b-8d66-5295f1d286d2] [~accountid:712020:725616c0-4ddd-4ec8-8be6-5dac31847bca]

