column58:
On the latest OS12 nightly pairing of bluetooth audio devices fails. 

Changes made in [https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/LX8-5527|https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/LX8-5527|smart-link] seem to be the issue, firmwares built before this change don’t show the problematic behaviour.

*Steps to reproduce:*

* Install any version built after merge of LX8-5527
* open Terminal and login as user
* start{{bluetoothctl}} (all following commands inside bluetoothctl interactive shell)
* Start device discovery with {{scan on}}
* List available bluetooth devices with {{devices}}
* Try to connect bluetooth audio device with {{connect <MacAddress of device>}}
* Results in: {{Failed to connect: org.bluez.Error.Failed br-connection-profile-unavailable}}



*Remarks:*

* [https://forums.debian.net/viewtopic.php?t=155520|https://forums.debian.net/viewtopic.php?t=155520|smart-link] points to {{libspa-0.2-bluetooth}} missing being an issue, but since we have that library included it might be a configuration error.

{{user@REMOVEBEFOREFLIGHT:~$ get app.avd.sessions.avd0.sessioninfo.domain }}
{{.options.default-user}}

but should point to default-domain

In thirdparty.json files can be downloaded using https, http or ftp urls.

Many download servers do a redirect to a CDN. igelpkg fails to follow those.

Task:

* Use requests and a chunked file write

thirdparty.json

{noformat}[
  {
    "url": "https://code.visualstudio.com/sha/download?build=stable&os=linux-deb-x64",
    "dest": "",
    "licenses": [
      {
        "name": "MIT"
      }
    ]
  }
]
{noformat}

Task:

* name of downloaded file should be the final url e.g. [https://vscode.download.prss.microsoft.com/dbazure/download/stable/848b80aeb52026648a8ff9f7c45a9b0a80641e2e/code_1.100.2-1747260578_amd64.deb|https://vscode.download.prss.microsoft.com/dbazure/download/stable/848b80aeb52026648a8ff9f7c45a9b0a80641e2e/code_1.100.2-1747260578_amd64.deb]

