column58:
I ran into an issue while updating [philips speech|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIGAPP/repos/philips_speech/browse?at=refs%2Fheads%2Ffeature%2FAPPS-80-update-philips-speech-driver-app-to-version-13.2.3] ([APPS-80|https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/APPS-80]). At the moment the project has 4 {{.json}} files that are activated when the cwa virtual channel plugin is enabled, namely:

{noformat}philips_PSPHID2_config.json
philips_PSPHID_config.json
philips_SpeechMikeAudio_config.json
philips_SpeechMikeMixer_config.json{noformat}

In the new update, they introduced a new variant “pulse audio” with 2 libraries. If the pulse audio is in use, then the

{noformat}philips_SpeechMikeAudio_config.json
philips_SpeechMikeMixer_config.json{noformat}

Should be turned off and the new config files 

{noformat}philips_SpeechMikeAudioPulse_config.json
philips_SpeechMikeMixerPulse_config.json{noformat}

Should be turned on. I created the aforementioned config files and added them to the project, they are an exact copy of the {{philips_SpeechMikeAudio_config.json}} and the {{philips_SpeechMikeMixerPulse_config.json}} besides the {{LIB_NAME}} field which holds a different property, fore example: ({{libCtxMixerAlsa.so}} and {{libCtxMixerPulse.so}}).

----

When I install the application (only added the {{.json}} files to the project), I inspect the {{module.ini}} and see 

{noformat}[SpeechMikeMixer]
DriverName = VDPSPMIX.dll
LIB_DIR = /services/philips_speech/usr/lib/PhilipsSpeech
LIB_NAME = libCtxMixerPulse.so{noformat}

An incorrect {{LIB_NAME}} is shown…

----

In the {{igel-philips-config.service}} it is running:


{noformat}/usr/share/app-integration/scripts/virtual_channel_config app.philips_speech.devices.cwa_enabled "cwa/philips_PSPHID_config.json,cwa/philips_PSPHID2_config.json,cwa/philips_SpeechMikeAudio_config.json,cwa/philips_SpeechMikeMixer_config.json" /services/cwa/usr/sbin/config.py module{noformat}

Note: {{cwa/philips_SpeechMikeMixer_config.json}}
And the content of this file:


{noformat}{
    "enabled": true,
    "module": {
        "virtualdriver": {
            "SpeechMikeMixer": {
                "DriverName": "/services/philips_speech/ica/ICAClient/VDPSPMIX.dll",
                "LIB_DIR": "/services/philips_speech/usr/lib/PhilipsSpeech",
                "LIB_NAME": "libCtxMixerAlsa.so"
            }
        }
    }
}{noformat}

The {{LIB_NAME}} has the {{libCtxMixerAlsa.so}} value and NOT {{libCtxMixerPulse.so}}. I assume since both config files have the {{[SpeechMikeMixer]}} as the virtual driver name? then the second file is overwriting it (I never triggered it, it is not even mentioned in the node action).

