In the igel-system-tray module input, we have the events

* setSpeed
* SetMouseDoubleclickSpeed
* SetTouchpadSensitivity

These are send from frontend to backend
and expect a reply from backend to frontend.

The reply is defined as 

{noformat}(data: unknown){noformat}

But as any communication between backend and frontend via libigelwebkit happens with json-objects,
this *data* must be used like this:

{noformat}const eventReply = data as {success: boolean};
if (!eventReply) {
  console.error('Response from backend invalid.');
  return;
}
dispatch(
  <do-something>(
    eventReply.success ? <success-case> : <failed-case>
  )
);{noformat}

The json can contain more then the boolean, also a number, a string, etc..

Here the related code in the frontend:
[https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/frontend/input/src/state/app/slice.ts#111,116,130,136,149,154|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/frontend/input/src/state/app/slice.ts#111,116,130,136,149,154]



And the backend needs to send an actual reply on these events in the event-handlers.
Currently there is just no reply at all.
The connected event-handlers are void-lambda-functions.
The backend needs something like:

{noformat}#include <igel/serialize/Property.h>
#include <tuple>

class EventReply {
public:
    explicit EventReply(bool success): success(success) {}
    EventReply() = default;

    bool success;

    constexpr static auto properties = std::make_tuple(
        igel::serialize::property(&EventReply::success, "success")
    );
};{noformat}

The EventReply-object can contain more then a bool, also int, or string, etc…

To send the reply on the event, return an EventReply(<true-or-false>) in the event-handlers.

Here the related code in the backend:
[https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/backend/src/input_info/Window.cpp#39-44,76-82,111-118|https://itga-bitbucket.igel.local/projects/LXIG/repos/igel-system-tray/browse/backend/src/input_info/Window.cpp#39-44,76-82,111-118]



